From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eden PS4 <eden-ps4@localhost>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:20:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] null renderer: colour clears, DMA copies and 2D blits in
 software

The null rasterizer did nothing for clears and claimed DMA copies and 2D
blits as done. Colour clears are now written to emulated memory (block
linear or pitch, scissored, the common colour formats, channel masks for
8-bit formats), and DMA copies and 2D blits go to their engines' software
paths. What a program draws that way then shows in the null renderer's
CPU-composed frames. Depth and stencil clears and shader draws still do
nothing.
---
 .../renderer_null/null_rasterizer.cpp         | 253 +++++++++++++++++-
 .../renderer_null/null_rasterizer.h           |   4 +
 2 files changed, 253 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_null/null_rasterizer.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_null/null_rasterizer.cpp
index a5cda0f38..b9b0f2c7d 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_null/null_rasterizer.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_null/null_rasterizer.cpp
@@ -1,8 +1,15 @@
